Name: Apache Portable Runtime
Short Name: apr
URL: https://github.com/apache/apr
Version: 1.7.6
Date: 2025-05-16
Revision: 5c18df51a91bcb3807f78eb36841d4d2ccf5563d
Update Mechanism: Manual
License: Apache-2.0, BSD-3-Clause, ISC, dso, Zlib
License File: LICENSE
Security Critical: no
Shipped: no
The library is not security critical because it is used for tests only.
Do not link it into production code.

Description:
   The Apache Portable Runtime Library provides a predictable and
   consistent interface to underlying platform-specific
   implementations, with an API to which software developers may code
   and be assured of predictable if not identical behavior regardless
   of the platform on which their software is built, relieving them of
   the need to code special-case conditions to work around or take
   advantage of platform-specific deficiencies or features.

Local Modifications:
src/ is a pristine checkout of the upstream Git repository at the release
tag. include/apr.h and include/arch/unix/apr_private.h are generated by
upstream's ./configure, so they are checked in outside src/. They were
generated on Linux and then edited for Android by apply_android_edits.py,
which disables what Android lacks (SCTP, SysV IPC, shm_open(), OS UUIDs,
glibc-specific functions) or what older API levels lack (getrandom(); APR
reads /dev/urandom instead), and some functions that older NDKs lacked.

To update:
1. Roll src/ in DEPS to the new release tag, and update Version, Date and
   Revision.
2. Download the release tarball (it includes ./configure) from
   https://apr.apache.org/download.cgi, extract it and run ./configure.
3. Copy include/apr.h and include/arch/unix/apr_private.h from it to
   include/ here, then run:
     ./apply_android_edits.py include/apr.h include/arch/unix/apr_private.h
4. Add new Unix sources to BUILD.gn (see OBJECTS_unix in the tarball's
   build-outputs.mk), and build //third_party/netty-tcnative for Android
   (is_cronet_build = true) for arm and arm64.
